{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-36015" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Identify the surface $4{x}^{2}+8{y}^{2}+2{z}^{2}-8x+8z+4=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049493/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6ba53532d14403202a523293b147fcdaf54598ca6580f0fe43dfc1f2f4bdc"} {"question" "q-36015" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we complete the square in the $x$ and $z$ terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}+8{y}^{2}+2{z}^{2}-8x+8z+4 & =0 \\\\ 4({x}^{2}-2x)+8{y}^{2}+2({z}^{2}+4z)+4 & =0 \\\\ 4[(x-1)^{2}-1]+8{y}^{2}+2[(z+2)^{2}-4]+4 & =0 \\\\ 4(x-1)^{2}-4+8{y}^{2}+2(z+2)^{2}-8+4 & =0 \\\\ 4(x-1)^{2}+8{y}^{2}+2(z+2)^{2}-8 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, by rearranging, we get the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(x-1)^{2}+8{y}^{2}+2(z+2)^{2}-8 & =0 \\\\ 4(x-1)^{2}+8{y}^{2}+2(z+2)^{2} & =8 \\\\ \\frac{4(x-1)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{8{y}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{2(z+2)^{2}}{8} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{2}+{y}^{2}+\\frac{(z+2)^{2}}{4} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the equation of an ellipsoid centered at $(1,0,-2).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049493/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6ba53532d14403202a523293b147fcdaf54598ca6580f0fe43dfc1f2f4bdc"} {"question" "q-36015" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049493/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "747d93087f5dd1927de8342cd960332b92bc58ae20a0c349634396e8beb3000c"} {"question" "q-36015" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049493/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6ba53532d14403202a523293b147fcdaf54598ca6580f0fe43dfc1f2f4bdc"} {"question" "q-36015" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "A hyperboloid of one sheet centered at $(1,0,-2)$"] ["text" "A hyperboloid of two sheets centered at $(1,0,-2)$"] ["text" "An ellipsoid centered at $(-1,0,2)$"] ["text" "An ellipsoid centered at $(1,0,-2)$"] ["text" "An ellipsoid centered at $(1,0,2)$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049493/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6ba53532d14403202a523293b147fcdaf54598ca6580f0fe43dfc1f2f4bdc"} {"question" "q-36015" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "An ellipsoid centered at $(1,0,-2)$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049493/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6ba53532d14403202a523293b147fcdaf54598ca6580f0fe43dfc1f2f4bdc"} {"question" "q-164543" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Identify the following surface:\n\n$$\n4{y}^{2}-3{z}^{2}=1,\\,-\\infty <x<\\infty .\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049493/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6ba53532d14403202a523293b147fcdaf54598ca6580f0fe43dfc1f2f4bdc"} {"question" "q-164543" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the equation of a hyperbolic cylinder whose axis of symmetry is the $z$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nThus, a hyperbolic cylinder whose axis of symmetry is the $x$**-axis** is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{{c}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our equation is a hyperbolic cylinder whose axis of symmetry is the $x$-axis and $b=\\frac{1}{2},\\,c=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049493/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6ba53532d14403202a523293b147fcdaf54598ca6580f0fe43dfc1f2f4bdc"} {"question" "q-164543" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049493/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "747d93087f5dd1927de8342cd960332b92bc58ae20a0c349634396e8beb3000c"} {"question" "q-164543" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049493/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6ba53532d14403202a523293b147fcdaf54598ca6580f0fe43dfc1f2f4bdc"} {"question" "q-164543" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "A hyperbolic cylinder whose axis of symmetry is the $x$-axis"] ["text" "A hyperbolic cylinder whose axis of symmetry is the $y$-axis"] ["text" "An elliptic cone whose axis of symmetry is the $y$-axis"] ["text" "An elliptic cylinder whose axis of symmetry is the $x$-axis"] ["text" "An elliptic cylinder whose axis of symmetry is the $y$-axis"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049493/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6ba53532d14403202a523293b147fcdaf54598ca6580f0fe43dfc1f2f4bdc"} {"question" "q-164543" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "A hyperbolic cylinder whose axis of symmetry is the $x$-axis"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049493/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6ba53532d14403202a523293b147fcdaf54598ca6580f0fe43dfc1f2f4bdc"} {"question" "q-164546" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Identify the following surface:\n\n$$\n{z}^{2}=8x,\\,-\\infty <y<\\infty .\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049493/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6ba53532d14403202a523293b147fcdaf54598ca6580f0fe43dfc1f2f4bdc"} {"question" "q-164546" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that the equation of a parabolic cylinder whose axis is the $z$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}=4py.\n$$\n\nThus, a parabolic cylinder whose axis is the $y$**-axis** is given by\n\n$$\n{z}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our equation is a parabolic cylinder whose axis is the $y$-axis and $p=2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049493/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6ba53532d14403202a523293b147fcdaf54598ca6580f0fe43dfc1f2f4bdc"} {"question" "q-164546" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049493/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "747d93087f5dd1927de8342cd960332b92bc58ae20a0c349634396e8beb3000c"} {"question" "q-164546" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049493/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6ba53532d14403202a523293b147fcdaf54598ca6580f0fe43dfc1f2f4bdc"} {"question" "q-164546" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "A couple of planes"] ["text" "A hyperbolic cylinder whose axis is the $x$-axis"] ["text" "A hyperbolic cylinder whose axis is the $y$-axis"] ["text" "A parabolic cylinder whose axis is the $x$-axis"] ["text" "A parabolic cylinder whose axis is the $y$-axis"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049493/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6ba53532d14403202a523293b147fcdaf54598ca6580f0fe43dfc1f2f4bdc"} {"question" "q-164546" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "A parabolic cylinder whose axis is the $y$-axis"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049493/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6ba53532d14403202a523293b147fcdaf54598ca6580f0fe43dfc1f2f4bdc"} {"question" "q-164553" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Identify the surface $5{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}-5{z}^{2}+20x+10z+15=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049493/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6ba53532d14403202a523293b147fcdaf54598ca6580f0fe43dfc1f2f4bdc"} {"question" "q-164553" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we complete the square in the $x$ and $z$ terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}-5{z}^{2}+20x+10z+15 & =0 \\\\ 5({x}^{2}+4x)-{y}^{2}-5({z}^{2}-2z)+15 & =0 \\\\ 5[(x+2)^{2}-4]-{y}^{2}-5[(z-1)^{2}-1]+15 & =0 \\\\ 5(x+2)^{2}-20-{y}^{2}-5(z-1)^{2}+5+15 & =0 \\\\ 5(x+2)^{2}-{y}^{2}-5(z-1)^{2} & =0 \\\\ -5(x+2)^{2}+{y}^{2}+5(z-1)^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the equation of an elliptic cone centered at $(-2,0,1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049493/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6ba53532d14403202a523293b147fcdaf54598ca6580f0fe43dfc1f2f4bdc"} {"question" "q-164553" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049493/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "747d93087f5dd1927de8342cd960332b92bc58ae20a0c349634396e8beb3000c"} {"question" "q-164553" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049493/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6ba53532d14403202a523293b147fcdaf54598ca6580f0fe43dfc1f2f4bdc"} {"question" "q-164553" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "A hyperboloid of one sheet centered at $(-2,0,1)$"] ["text" "A hyperboloid of two sheet centered at $(-2,0,1)$"] ["text" "An elliptic cone centered at $(-2,0,-1)$"] ["text" "An elliptic cone centered at $(-2,0,1)$"] ["text" "An elliptic cone centered at $(-2,1,1)$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049493/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6ba53532d14403202a523293b147fcdaf54598ca6580f0fe43dfc1f2f4bdc"} {"question" "q-164553" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "An elliptic cone centered at $(-2,0,1)$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049493/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6ba53532d14403202a523293b147fcdaf54598ca6580f0fe43dfc1f2f4bdc"} {"question" "q-164554" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Identify the surface $2{x}^{2}-4{z}^{2}-4x-y-16z-12=0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049493/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6ba53532d14403202a523293b147fcdaf54598ca6580f0fe43dfc1f2f4bdc"} {"question" "q-164554" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we complete the square in the $x$ and $z$ terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}-4{z}^{2}-4x-y-16z-12 & =0 \\\\ 2({x}^{2}-2x)-4({z}^{2}+4z)-y-12 & =0 \\\\ 2[(x-1)^{2}-1]-4[(z+2)^{2}-4]-y-12 & =0 \\\\ 2(x-1)^{2}-2-4(z+2)^{2}+16-y-12 & =0 \\\\ 2(x-1)^{2}-4(z+2)^{2}-y+2 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, by rearranging, we get the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x-1)^{2}-4(z+2)^{2}-y+2 & =0 \\\\ 2(x-1)^{2}-4(z+2)^{2} & =y-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the equation of a hyperbolic paraboloid centered at $(1,2,-2).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049493/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6ba53532d14403202a523293b147fcdaf54598ca6580f0fe43dfc1f2f4bdc"} {"question" "q-164554" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049493/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "747d93087f5dd1927de8342cd960332b92bc58ae20a0c349634396e8beb3000c"} {"question" "q-164554" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049493/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6ba53532d14403202a523293b147fcdaf54598ca6580f0fe43dfc1f2f4bdc"} {"question" "q-164554" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "A hyperbolic paraboloid centered at $(-1,-2,2).$"] ["text" "A hyperbolic paraboloid centered at $(1,2,-2).$"] ["text" "An elliptic cone centered at $(1,2,-2).$"] ["text" "An elliptic paraboloid centered at $(-1,-2,2)$"] ["text" "An elliptic paraboloid centered at $(1,2,-2)$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14049493/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6ba53532d14403202a523293b147fcdaf54598ca6580f0fe43df